<https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1990/40/eng@/~cl_4__para_c> <https://schema.org/text> "by inserting after paragraph (e) of subsection (5) the following new paragraph (f): \"(f) on the ground that the employee had, for the purpose of his appointment to the service of a statutory or local authority;— (i) made any statement or given any information, whether orally or writing, whether on oath or otherwise; or (ii) supplied any document, which was false, erroneous, inaccurate, in- complete, or misleading or likely to mislead, and his appointment into the service of a statutory or local authority was made partly or wholly in reliance on that statement, information or document: Provided that retirement under this para- graph shall not be effected unless the PENSIONS (AMENDMENT) employee has been given a reasonable opportunity to make representations thereon to the said appropriate authority.\"; and"@en <https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1990/40/eng@> .
